{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sin(x)^2\n  ucas: diff it x\nd/dx it = 2sin(x)*cos(x)\n  holds for every real x\n  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-14)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the derivative of (sin x)^2 with respect to x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = sin(x)^2", "diff it x"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "diff", "vars": ["x"], "order": 1, "derivative": "2sin(x)*cos(x)"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 201, "max_diff": 2.8055086465778034e-14, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sin(x)^2\n  ucas: diff it x\nd/dx it = 2sin(x)*cos(x)\n  holds for every real x\n  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-14)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x, y) = x^2 + y^2\n  ucas: grad it at 1, 2\n∇ it = (2x, 2y)\n  ∂/∂x it = 2x\n  ∂/∂y it = 2y\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 4e-13)\n  at (x = 1, y = 2): (2, 4), |∇| = 4.472135955\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the gradient of x^2 + y^2 at (1, 2)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x, y) = x^2 + y^2", "grad it at 1, 2"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "grad", "gradient": [{"var": "x", "derivative": "2x"}, {"var": "y", "derivative": "2y"}], "at_value": [2, 4], "at_norm": 4.47213595499958}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 200, "max_diff": 3.9970424744006895e-13, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x, y) = x^2 + y^2\n  ucas: grad it at 1, 2\n∇ it = (2x, 2y)\n  ∂/∂x it = 2x\n  ∂/∂y it = 2y\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 4e-13)\n  at (x = 1, y = 2): (2, 4), |∇| = 4.472135955\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "d/dx sin(x)^2 = 2sin(x)*cos(x)\n  holds for every real x\n  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-14)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "diff", "ucas": "diff sin(x)^2 x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "diff", "vars": ["x"], "order": 1, "derivative": "2sin(x)*cos(x)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 201, "max_diff": 2.8055086465778034e-14, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "d/dx sin(x)^2 = 2sin(x)*cos(x)\n  holds for every real x\n  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-14)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "∫ x dx\n  = x^2/2 + C\n  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 3.14159] (max difference 0)\n  from 0 to 3.14159: F(3.14159) - F(0) = 4.93480220054468\n  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 4.93480220054468, estimated error 5.4e-14\n  the two agree to 8.9e-16\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "integrate", "ucas": "integrate x wrt x from 0 to pi", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "integrate", "var": "x", "integrand": "x", "antiderivative": "x^2/2", "definite": {"from": 0, "to": 3.141592653589793, "symbolic": 4.934802200544679, "numeric": 4.93480220054468, "error_estimate": 5.428282420599148e-14, "evaluations": 15, "value": 4.934802200544679}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "derivative", "points": 401, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "d/dx of the antiderivative against the integrand"}, {"kind": "numeric_integral", "points": 15, "max_diff": 8.881784197001252e-16, "passed": true, "text": "F(b) - F(a) against adaptive Gauss-Kronrod"}], "files": [], "text": "∫ x dx\n  = x^2/2 + C\n  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 3.14159] (max difference 0)\n  from 0 to 3.14159: F(3.14159) - F(0) = 4.93480220054468\n  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 4.93480220054468, estimated error 5.4e-14\n  the two agree to 8.9e-16\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sin(x)\n  ucas: taylor it order 5\nMaclaurin (Taylor at 0) series of it at x = 0, through order 5:\n  it = x - x^3/6 + x^5/120 + O(x^6)\n  as x -> 0; coefficients c_k = f^(k)(0)/k!: 0 1 0 -1/6 0 1/120\n  check: the coefficients agree with Taylor-jet arithmetic (long double) to 0\n  check: |f - P| = 1.98e-11 at x = 0 ± 1/10, 1.55e-13 at ± 1/20, 1.21e-15 at ± 1/40 (shrinks like h^7.0; expected >= 6)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the taylor series of sin x about 0 to order 5", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = sin(x)", "taylor it order 5"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "taylor", "var": "x", "at": 0, "order": 5, "polynomial": "x - x^3/6 + x^5/120", "coefficients": ["0", "1", "0", "-1/6", "0", "1/120"]}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "taylor_jet", "points": 6, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "coefficients against long double Taylor-jet arithmetic"}], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = sin(x)\n  ucas: taylor it order 5\nMaclaurin (Taylor at 0) series of it at x = 0, through order 5:\n  it = x - x^3/6 + x^5/120 + O(x^6)\n  as x -> 0; coefficients c_k = f^(k)(0)/k!: 0 1 0 -1/6 0 1/120\n  check: the coefficients agree with Taylor-jet arithmetic (long double) to 0\n  check: |f - P| = 1.98e-11 at x = 0 ± 1/10, 1.55e-13 at ± 1/20, 1.21e-15 at ± 1/40 (shrinks like h^7.0; expected >= 6)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)\nsum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)\n  converges absolutely: p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1\n  = pi^2/6\n  method: partial fractions; zeta(k), digamma at integers\n  numeric: 1.644934066848226 (the first 128 terms plus an Euler-Maclaurin tail (integral + 3 corrections); estimated error 4.4e-16)\n  check: the closed form and the numeric value agree (difference 4.4e-16)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the sum of 1/n^2 from 1 to infinity", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "infinite_sum", "converges_absolutely": "p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1", "value": "pi^2/6", "method": "partial fractions; zeta(k), digamma at integers", "numeric": "1.644934066848226 (the first 128 terms plus an Euler-Maclaurin tail (integral + 3 corrections); estimated error 4.4e-16)", "headline": "sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the closed form and the numeric value agree (difference 4.4e-16)"}], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: sum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)\nsum(n, 1, inf, 1/n^2)\n  converges absolutely: p-series 1/n^2 with p = 2 > 1\n  = pi^2/6\n  method: partial fractions; zeta(k), digamma at integers\n  numeric: 1.644934066848226 (the first 128 terms plus an Euler-Maclaurin tail (integral + 3 corrections); estimated error 4.4e-16)\n  check: the closed form and the numeric value agree (difference 4.4e-16)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "limit of sin(x)/x as x -> 0:\n  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(1) = lim cos(x)\n  = 1 (from both sides)\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "limit", "ucas": "limit sin(x)/x as x -> 0", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "limit", "var": "x", "at": "0", "side": "both", "limit": {"kind": "number", "value": 1, "text": "1"}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "numeric_left", "points": 22, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "Richardson-extrapolated values approaching the point"}, {"kind": "numeric_right", "points": 22, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "Richardson-extrapolated values approaching the point"}], "files": [], "text": "limit of sin(x)/x as x -> 0:\n  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(1) = lim cos(x)\n  = 1 (from both sides)\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n"}, "isError": false}}
